    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_19a2d5c4b7bfa41571fc37ab7d21d9b02e6fe28575dff2b352e55e5824587ab8",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Across the family sketches, the reusable prime-polynomial and tail-bound architecture must be recentered according to the coherent prime-square layer: quadratic Dirichlet values acquire a positive half-log-log shift, whereas elliptic-curve twists acquire a negative half-log-log shift, matching the later conjectural positive and negative Gaussian centers; primitive characters retain the transferred architecture and are assigned zero conjectural center.",
